            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nIt looks like an expected behavior of 'mini.ai' default textobject. It is designed to [treat input characters as a separator](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/9990c41f10f54f29a888d13024c9f765037bde23/doc/mini-ai.txt#L174-L176) and not \"enclosing\" character. For this reason only the right edge is included by default. You can see that after `va.` in the example from the issue the left `.` is not selected.\n\nThis default behavior allows for a more straightforward \"delete part between separators\" case. The logic here is that the \"enclosing\" characters usually either have different left/right parts or are balanced. Which is not true for default fallback (when the character is unknown for 'mini.ai' and the user).",
